        <briefdescription>
<para>zero-coupon inflation rate. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Essentially the fair rate for a zero-coupon inflation swap (by definition), i.e. the zero term structure uses yearly compounding, which is assumed for ZCIIS instrument quotes.</para><para><simplesect kind="note"><para>by default you get the same as lag and interpolation as the term structure. If you want to get predictions of RPI/CPI/etc then use an index. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
